  "text": "我们需要回答用户中文请求：详细设计基于 Raft 的分布式键值数据库，依次说明日志复制、选举、持久化、快照、成员变更、线性一致性读取、故障恢复及测试。给出伪代码和具体故障时序，逐步论证安全性与活性。\n\n需要产出详尽中文技术设计。必须包含伪代码、故障时序、安全性活性论证。需要覆盖 Raft 核心：日志复制、选举、持久化、快照、成员变更、线性一致性读取、故障恢复、测试。可能还要键值数据库状态机：命令 Get/Put/Delete/Transaction? 线性一致性读取可以用 ReadIndex 或 Lease Read。需要详细。\n\n需要确保最终答案结构清晰。可能包括：\n- 总体架构：节点、RPC、状态机、日志、存储、客户端。\n- 数据结构：Term, votedFor, log entries, commitIndex, lastApplied, state, peers, config, snapshot, lastIncludedIndex/Term, applied KV map, pending reads.\n- RPC: RequestVote, AppendEntries, InstallSnapshot, ReadIndex? ClientRequest.\n- 日志复制：leader 接收命令，append log, replicate, majority commit, apply. 伪代码。\n- 选举：follower timeout, candidate, RequestVote, majority, become leader. 伪代码。\n- 持久化：WAL, fsync, checkpoint, atomic rename, crash consistency. 伪代码。\n- 快照：触发条件，生成 snapshot, InstallSnapshot, 截断日志。伪代码。\n- 成员变更：单步变更 Joint consensus / 两阶段。伪代码。\n- 线性一致性读：ReadIndex: leader确认自己仍是leader，等待 commitIndex >= readIndex，apply 到 readIndex 后读。或 Lease Read。伪代码。\n- 故障恢复：启动恢复，从持久化日志/快照重建，选举，日志匹配，提交。\n- 测试：单元、集成、故障注入、线性一致性检查（Jepsen-like）、混沌、性能。\n- 具体故障时序：网络分区、leader crash、follower crash、磁盘故障、成员变更期间故障、快照传输故障、读请求故障。\n- 安全性与活性论证：选举安全性（最多一个 leader per term）、日志匹配、状态机安全性、选举限制、成员变更安全性、线性一致性读安全性、活性（leader选举、日志复制、读）。\n\n需要可能包含伪代码语言风格。\n\n需要注意：用户要求“依次说明日志复制、选举、持久化、快照、成员变更、线性一致性读取、故障恢复及测试。” 可以按这个顺序。但总体架构先给。\n\n需要详细，可能很长。 Desired oververbosity 9. 需要中文。\n\n让我们规划最终答案：\n\n标题：基于 Raft 的分布式键值数据库设计\n\n0. 设计目标与约束\n- 强一致线性一致性，多数派，容错 f 节点容忍 f 故障，2f+1。\n- 命令：Put(key,value), Delete(key), Get(key), maybe CAS/Tx.\n- 状态机：KV map + version.\n\n1. 总体架构\n- 节点模块：ClientService, RaftCore, LogStore, StateMachine, SnapshotStore, Transport.\n- 数据结构伪代码。\n\n2. 日志复制\n- Entry: {term, index, command, checksum}\n- Leader flow: receive command, append, replicate, commit, apply.\n- AppendEntries RPC: prevLogIndex/Term, entries, leaderCommit.\n- Follower consistency check, truncate, append, update commit, apply.\n- 伪代码: client_command, replicate, append_entries_handler, apply_committed.\n- 故障时序：leader发送部分复制后crash，新leader补全。\n\n3. 选举\n- 随机超时，candidate, RequestVote, vote rules, majority.\n- 伪代码: election_timeout, request_vote_handler.\n- 故障时序：双 leader? 网络分区，旧 leader 被隔离，新 leader 选举，旧 leader 发现更高 term 降级。\n\n4. 持久化\n- WAL: append before send? 通常 append to log then fsync before AppendEntries? Raft论文: append to log before sending; fsync before commit? For durability, fsync before applying and before responding? Need robust: append to WAL with fsync before sending AppendEntries or at least before commit. To avoid losing committed entries, leader must fsync entries before counting as replicated? Actually follower must fsync before ack? For safety, committed entries must be durable on majority before commit. If follower acks before fsync and crashes, leader may commit based on volatile ack, then leader crashes, new leader may not have entry -> lost. So follower should fsync before ack, or leader only commit after majority durable. We can specify fsync before ack. Also leader fsync before apply? If leader crashes after commit but before apply, can recover from log. Need fsync commitIndex? commitIndex can be volatile but must be recoverable? If leader commits and applies, then crashes before fsync commitIndex, on restart it may not know commitIndex; but can recompute? It can set commitIndex=lastApplied? But if applied entries not durable? State machine snapshot? Need ensure applied state durable or log durable. Simpler: fsync WAL before ack; leader fsync WAL before apply; persist commitIndex periodically but can recover by scanning? In Raft, commitIndex volatile; if leader crashes after commit but before applying, new leader may have committed entries in log; but if old leader restarts, it may not know commitIndex. It can set commitIndex=lastApplied? But if it had applied entries but not persisted lastApplied, could reapply? State machine apply must be idempotent or use appliedIndex persisted. Need design: persist lastApplied with fsync after applying batch, or use snapshot. On restart, lastApplied from durable. commitIndex can be initialized to lastApplied; leader will learn commitIndex from majority via AppendEntries? Actually if leader restarts, it may not know committed entries; but it can set commitIndex=lastApplied and then as leader, it can commit entries when replicated to majority. But if entries already committed by previous leader and not applied, new leader can commit them again? If they are in log and replicated to majority, leader can advance commitIndex by matching. If old leader restarts as follower, leader will send commitIndex. If old leader restarts as leader, it can recommit committed entries if majority has them. But if it doesn't know commitIndex, it can still commit when majority acks. Need ensure no loss. We can specify WAL fsync before ack, leader fsync before apply, persist lastApplied atomically with state machine or WAL. For simplicity: fsync WAL before sending AppendEntries ack; leader fsync WAL before applying; persist lastApplied after apply; commitIndex volatile but can be recovered from leader's AppendEntries or recomputed by leader using majority acks.\n\n- 伪代码: append_log, fsync, apply_batch.\n- 故障时序：follower ack before fsync bug导致丢失；正确设计避免。\n\n5. 快照\n- 触发：log size > threshold or time.\n- 生成：take snapshot of applied state at lastApplied, persist snapshot meta, truncate log.\n- InstallSnapshot RPC: lastIncludedIndex/Term, data.\n- 伪代码: maybe_snapshot, install_snapshot_handler.\n- 故障时序：leader发送快照，follower crash，重启后重新发送；快照损坏校验。\n\n6. 成员变更\n- 单步变更不安全，使用 joint consensus: C_old,new. 两阶段：进入 joint, 再退出 joint.\n- 配置变更作为日志命令。\n- 选举和提交 majority 定义：joint 中需要同时多数派 old 和 new。\n- 伪代码: change_membership, joint_majority, request_vote/append_entries use current config.\n- 故障时序：joint 阶段 leader crash，新 leader 继续 joint；退出阶段故障。\n\n7. 线性一致性读取\n- 方案：ReadIndex。Leader 记录 readIndex=commitIndex，确认自己仍是 leader（心跳或 lease），等待 apply >= readIndex，读状态机。\n- 伪代码: read_index, read_index_handler, wait_apply.\n- Lease read optional: leader lease, clock drift.\n- 故障时序：leader网络分区，旧 leader 不能确认，拒绝读；新 leader 提供读。\n\n8. 故障恢复\n- 启动流程：load snapshot, replay log, set term/votedFor, start election timeout.\n- 日志匹配：leader sends AppendEntries with nextIndex, decrement on conflict.\n- 伪代码: recover, match_log.\n- 故障时序：多数派同时 crash? 恢复；单节点重启；leader crash。\n\n9. 测试\n- 单元：日志匹配、选举、快照、成员变更。\n- 集成：网络分区、延迟、丢包、磁盘故障、时钟漂移。\n- 线性一致性：Jepsen-like, history checker, Knossos.\n- 故障注入：kill -9, fsync failure, partial write, RPC duplicate/reorder.\n- 混沌：随机故障，长时间运行。\n- 性能：吞吐、延迟、leader切换。\n- 测试矩阵。\n\n10. 安全性与活性论证\n- Safety:\n  - Election Safety: at most one leader per term due to votedFor and majority.\n  - Leader Completeness: leader has all committed entries due to election restriction (up-to-date).\n  - Log Matching: if two logs have same term/index, same command and all previous same.\n  - State Machine Safety: committed entries same order applied.\n  - Membership Safety: joint consensus ensures no two leaders with conflicting configs? Need argue.\n  - Linearizable Read: ReadIndex ensures read reflects committed state and no stale leader.\n- Liveness:\n  - Leader election: random timeouts, eventual leader if network stable.\n  - Log replication: leader replicates to majority, commit.\n  - Read liveness: leader can confirm and apply.\n  - Membership liveness: joint changes complete.\n- 故障时序逐步论证 maybe integrated.\n\nNeed include specific failure timelines. Could have table with time steps.\n\nNeed be careful with pseudo-code not too long but detailed.\n\nPotential final structure:\n\n- 引言\n- 1. 系统模型与数据结构\n- 2. 日志复制\n- 3. 选举\n- 4. 持久化\n- 5. 快照\n- 6. 成员变更\n- 7. 线性一致性读取\n- 8. 故障恢复\n- 9. 测试\n- 10. 安全性与活性论证\n- 11. 关键故障时序汇总\n\nBut user says 依次说明... maybe order exactly. Could do each section with 伪代码 + 故障时序 + 安全性/活性. Then final overall proof.\n\nNeed include pseudo-code for each.\n\nLet's design details.\n\nSystem model:\n- Cluster N=2f+1.\n- RPC reliable with possible loss/delay/duplicate, no corruption? We can add checksum.\n- Clocks not synchronized for lease; ReadIndex doesn't rely on clock.\n- Client requests idempotent? For linearizable KV, commands can be idempotent? Put/Delete idempotent. Get read-only. For retries, need client request id to avoid duplicate side effects? Put idempotent, Delete idempotent. If transactions, need dedup. We can mention command idempotency or dedup table.\n\nData structures:\n```\nenum Role {FOLLOWER, CANDIDATE, LEADER}\nstruct Entry {\n  term: int\n  index: int\n  cmd: Command // Put(key,val), Delete(key), ConfigChange(newConfig), Noop\n  checksum: bytes\n}\nstruct Snapshot {\n  lastIncludedIndex: int\n  lastIncludedTerm: int\n  config: Config\n  data: KVMap\n  checksum: bytes\n}\nstruct Node {\n  role, currentTerm, votedFor\n  log: LogStore\n  commitIndex, lastApplied\n  peers, nextIndex, matchIndex\n  config: Config // current membership\n  jointConfig: Config? // old,new\n  stateMachine: KVMap\n  snapshotStore\n  readIndex, pendingReads\n}\n```\n\nRPC:\n```\nRequestVote(term, candidateId, lastLogIndex, lastLogTerm) -> term, voteGranted\nAppendEntries(term, leaderId, prevLogIndex, prevLogTerm, entries, leaderCommit) -> term, success, matchIndex\nInstallSnapshot(term, leaderId, lastIncludedIndex, lastIncludedTerm, offset, data, done) -> term, success\nReadIndex(term, leaderId) -> term, readIndex, success? maybe leader confirms.\n```\n\nClient:\n```\nPut(key,value), Delete(key), Get(key)\n```\n\nLog replication pseudo:\n```\non_client_command(cmd):\n  if role != LEADER: forward to leader\n  entry = {term: currentTerm, index: log.lastIndex+1, cmd}\n  log.append(entry)\n  fsync(log)\n  nextIndex[peers] = log.lastIndex+1\n  replicate()\n  wait until commitIndex >= entry.index\n  apply up to entry.index\n  return result\n\nreplicate():\n  for peer in peers:\n    send AppendEntries(peer, nextIndex[peer])\n\non_append_entries(req):\n  if req.term < currentTerm: return false\n  if req.term > currentTerm: step_down(req.term)\n  reset_election_timer()\n  if !log.exists(req.prevLogIndex, req.prevLogTerm): return false\n  truncate log after req.prevLogIndex\n  append missing entries with fsync\n  if req.leaderCommit > commitIndex:\n     commitIndex = min(req.leaderCommit, log.lastIndex)\n     apply_committed()\n  return true, log.lastIndex\n```\n\nNeed handle snapshot: if prevLogIndex < snapshot.lastIncludedIndex, return false with hint? Or InstallSnapshot.\n\nElection pseudo:\n```\nelection_timeout():\n  if role == LEADER: return\n  currentTerm++\n  role = CANDIDATE\n  votedFor = self\n ",
